---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Simply Plant Care"
  description="What Simply Plant Care is, who it helps, and how its guides are researched."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">About</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1>About Simply Plant Care</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Simply Plant Care is a small website about one thing: keeping
      houseplants alive. It was started because most plant advice falls into
      two unhelpful camps — vague ("water when needed") or technical enough
      to need a botany degree. We try to sit in the middle: clear, practical
      instructions a beginner can follow, with enough of the "why" to help
      you make your own decisions later.
    </p>
    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>
      People who have just bought their first plant, people who have killed
      a few and want to know why, and anyone who wants a straight answer to
      a specific question — how often to water a snake plant, whether a ZZ
      plant really copes with low light, or what to do about brown leaf tips.
    </p>
    <h2>How the content is researched</h2>
    <p>
      Every guide is written from general horticultural knowledge and
      checked against public references from university extension services
      and botanical gardens. We do not copy content from other websites. When
      a topic is genuinely debated — for example, whether misting helps
      humidity — we say so rather than pretending there is one settled
      answer.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      We are not a nursery, we do not sell plants, and we are not a
      substitute for professional advice. Our guides cover common houseplants
      and common problems; unusual or valuable plants may need specialist
      care. If you have a question or think a guide is wrong, please
      <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> — corrections are welcome.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
